types of software
1.System software
2.Application software

1.System s/w
It is used to manage system hardware(physical components like cpu,monitor ,keyboard etc)and application software.
eg:os like woindows macos and linux.

2.it is a s/w performs only by taking instructions from end users
without os (system s/w) we can't run app s/w
eg: browser,word,paint,excalidraw etc..
Operating system 
An os is a type of system software which is used to manage sytem h/w and s/w resources
It acts as an interface between user and computer h/w
It provides an user interface and controls how applications and hardware communicate
windows os linux os and mac os
picture


Functionalities of Os
1.process management
2.Mempory management 
3.I/O Device management
4.File management
5.Network management
6.Security management
7.User management
8.Storage or disk management

1.process management(Running application)
a.which process will be executed
b.which process will be executed for how much time.
c.allocating proces to processor
d.deallocating process from processor

2.Memory management
For a program to process to get executed ,it requires memory 
a. how much memory to allocate to a process
b.deallocating memory from process 
c.how much memory is currently being used
d. how much memory is free

3.I/O management
we can connect multiple devices like mouse keyboard printer scanner etc
a.which process gets the device for how much time 
b.managing the connection of these devices

4.File management
file systems contain many files and directories that are well organised
keep track of 
a.information
b.location
c.users
d.status

5>Network management
Managing all network connections and devices

6.Security management
Managing all users
who is the authorized user
Restricting access to unauthorized users and activity

7.user management
Can create multiple users for a single machine and control the access

8.Storage management
storage maanagement is an operating system manages how data and files are stored
,organised and retrieved from storage devices like HDDs and SSDs

It manages disk space file systems directories and allocation of storage to programs
and users.

